igned}8 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ and $T(v)=[\\begin{aligned}48 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}],$ what is the standard matrix of $T?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088155 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7193e739-601b-592a-8f0d-83363b6d9331" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088155 #edb/ref 1074 "We can write $T(v)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =[\\begin{aligned}48 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =6\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =6v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $T(v)=6v,$ and so the linear transformation $T$ is a dilation with scale factor $k=6.$\n\nThe matrix that represents a dilation of scale factor $k$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}k & 0 \\\\ 0 & k\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix of $T$ is\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088554 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186088555 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088554 #edb/ref 1061 18547 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088554 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "218377cb-122a-56d3-9bc2-df2b7ebad88e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088554 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186088904 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088555 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186088560 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088555 #edb/ref 1061 18548 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088555 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "100ba475-df33-5ce4-9f19-dc90b51a15ac" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088555 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186087717 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088560 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186088561 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088560 #edb/ref 1061 18603 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088560 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5621dae4-d9c7-5199-b4f0-2ee503009aa1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088560 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186087721 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088561 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186088562 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088561 #edb/ref 1061 18604 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186088561 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a2b6d468-dc59-53d1-b89f